on, to: Position): void" style="text;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=4;spacingRight=4;overflow=hidden;rotatable=0;points=[[0,0.5],[1,0.5]];portConstraint=eastwest;html=1;" parent="c58" vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="48" width="340" height="22" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c61" value="+ close(): void" style="text;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=4;spacingRight=4;overflow=hidden;rotatable=0;points=[[0,0.5],[1,0.5]];portConstraint=eastwest;html=1;" parent="c58" vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="70" width="340" height="22" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c62" value="connection" style="endArrow=open;endSize=10;html=1;rounded=0;fontSize=10;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" parent="1" edge="1" source="c30" target="c58"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="c63" value="&lt;b&gt;Template Method (the existing design)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;checkChessmanMove() (GamePanel.java, lines 206–222) is the template:&lt;br&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;moveChessman(newPosition, _selected.pos);&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;opponentTurn();&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;opponentTurn() is the one abstract step. Each subclass fills it in, so the kind of opponent is fixed by which subclass Menu creates." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;fontSize=11;" parent="1" vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="1240" y="20" width="600" height="110" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c64" value="" style="endArrow=none;dashed=1;html=1;rounded=0;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=1;entryY=0.3;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" parent="1" edge="1" source="c63" target="c2"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="c65" value="The opponent is not only in opponentTurn():&lt;br&gt;- the colour and connection dialogs run in the constructors&lt;br&gt;- GamePanelLAN overrides moveChessman to send every local move, and calls super.moveChessman for received moves so they are not sent back&lt;br&gt;- undo/redo (Command) is overridden too: 1 move in hot-seat, 2 vs AI, a message in LAN" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;fontSize=11;" parent="1" vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="1620" y="420" width="260" height="170" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c66" value="" style="endArrow=none;dashed=1;html=1;rounded=0;exitX=0;exitY=0.3;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=1;entryY=0.25;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" parent="1" edge="1" source="c65" target="c30"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell><mxCell id="c67" value="Menu.java, lines 50–79: one button per subclass&lt;br&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;new GameFrame(new GamePanelHot());&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;new GameFrame(new GamePanelLAN());&lt;/font&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font face=&quot;Courier New&quot;&gt;new GameFrame(new GamePanelAI());&lt;/font&gt;" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=14;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;fontSize=11;" parent="1" vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="110" width="420" height="90" as="geometry"/></mxCell><mxCell id="c68" value="" style="endArrow=none;dashed=1;html=1;rounded=0;exitX=0.3;exitY=0;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0.3;entryY=1;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" parent="1" edge="1" source="c67" target="c47"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram></mxfile>